{"id":"454266265","kind":"article","title":"许多人认为记忆对深刻的创造性工作不重要","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zD5zaKmvTFAAL3PTJGWzkAQr6CtoBCdoXBpM"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2022-01-07","updated":"2025-07-30","votes":32,"comment_count":0,"minutes":2,"chars":942,"keywords":["间隔重复","长期记忆","创造力","组块","专业能力"],"summary":"短文回应“深度创造不需要记忆”的说法，列出记忆的重要性：基础认知依赖记忆，创新洞见依赖长期记忆，深刻理解需要扎实基础，专业能力依赖复杂组块。作者还认为间隔重复能让记忆自动化、腾出思考空间，并缩短学科入门阶段的挫败。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/454266265","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"参考文献"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"EMhi2f7g\">当告诉别人<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4bR1HVvDUhMXDm5SJB4Tiw4xGbrm9AfXWgbc\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统让记忆成为一种选择</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>时，人们往往反应相当消极：「背诵知识有什么意义？死知识才不是关键。我想要得到概念性的理解、创造力、艺术性，诸如此类！」</p><p data-pid=\"EIcko4He\">对此的一个回应是指出事实上<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6UZP7P4sRNgRKSvNj7tMV5uW6dDhwwbdZCy9\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统可以用来发展概念理解</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>。但记忆知识没有价值的说法也必须认真对待。在此我有些回应：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"u9IvXuqL\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zDTbondrBtJa2zzsn5u896MKQkAEY5HbJqmG\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">基本认知任务依赖于记忆</a></li><li data-pid=\"nf8mtiRP\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zNW5jyTpU1v4XBQfTYwoM8Q\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">一些创新洞察依赖于长期记忆</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup></li><li data-pid=\"fNswkQlq\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zQiumA4k3SXo1GeRVJpsrVaBRETAoyYmSERS\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">深刻的理解要求细致掌握基础知识</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup> </li><li data-pid=\"enjRkh08\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z7s7zpUDq2EEXnu3XJQLmqjddZnwGkBfz5WWL\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">专业水准需要建立复杂的组块重编码方案</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup></li><li data-pid=\"ykxgRoHi\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5d7PMFhoTTpJfGAXms4H9gSBvUDRHb43pkfn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">人们在学校经受过死记硬背，因由这些负面经历而低估记忆的重要性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup> </li><li data-pid=\"ukcYXF_8\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3hyucvGpCUB361PCegiHbX7FyFHcqZZF2pKK\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统让记忆更加自动化，从而有助于更深入的琢磨思考</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup></li><li data-pid=\"rCRh5HEC\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z36hoKonZMF93rY34goQhyFLfnTfHmSwBzNYs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统可以缩短科目学习中不愉快的早期阶段</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup><br/><br/> </li></ul><hr/><h2 id=\"sec-1\">参考文献</h2><p data-pid=\"HoAOYxOL\">Matuschak, A., &amp; Nielsen, M. (2019, October 0). <i>How can we develop transformative tools for thought?</i><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup> <a class=\"external\" href=\"https://numinous.productions/ttft\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"visible\">numinous.productions/tt</span><span class=\"invisible\">ft</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a> (see section “<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://numinous.productions/ttft/#how-important-is-memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">How important is memory anyway?</a>”)</p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"PrTmT9Dg\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">间隔重复记忆系统</a></li><li data-pid=\"5QvGklH6\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"400001519\" href=\"#/post/400001519\">人们似乎忘记了他们所读的大部分内容，而且他们大多没有注意到这一点</a></li><li data-pid=\"3_KTv8Nv\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"398045447\" href=\"#/post/398045447\">间隔重复记忆系统可用于发展概念性理解</a></li><li data-pid=\"eTFFDcdb\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"459483765\" href=\"#/post/459483765\">助记媒介 (Mnemonic medium)</a></li><li data-pid=\"q9iSd9HC\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"466828742\" href=\"#/post/466828742\">间隔重复记忆系统可以缩短科目学习中不愉快的早期阶段</a></li><li data-pid=\"BDJ9bnp-\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"468172742\" href=\"#/post/468172742\">间隔重复记忆系统让记忆更加自动化，从而有助于更深入的琢磨思考</a></li><li data-pid=\"bW_XOjug\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"490650748\" href=\"#/post/490650748\">人们在学校经受过死记硬背，因由这些负面经历而低估记忆的重要性</a></li><li data-pid=\"VrujkshK\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1933460394887868508\" href=\"#/post/1933460394887868508\">Kirschner, Sweller, &amp; Clark (2006)：《为什么最小化指导教学是无效的：对建构主义、发现式、问题导向、体验式和探究式教学失败的分析》</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-3\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"xHn7mPCd\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"n7_bO_mg\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zD5zaKmvTFAAL3PTJGWzkAQr6CtoBCdoXBpM\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Many people view memory as unimportant to deep creative work (andymatuschak.org)</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统使记忆成为一种选择 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397582470\" href=\"#/post/397582470\